    {
      "text": "UML class diagram in a frame tabbed 'Hardware profile'. Above the frame sit Core/ Specification and Core/ Element. ProductSpecification (hazard: DefinedType [0..*]) specialises Core/Specification. The abstract Hardware specialises Core/Element, with productAgent :Agent [1], hardwareVersion:xsd:string [0..1], partNumber : xsd:string [1], releaseDate :DateTime [0..1], serialNumber : xsd:string [0..1], batchNumber : xsd:string [0..1], hazard: DefinedType [0..*], category: DefinedType [0..*], additionalInformationSpecification : /Core/Specification [0..*] and additionalInformation :/Core/DictionaryEntry [0..*]. Three classes specialise Hardware: PhysicalHardware (massOfHardware: MeasureOfMass [0..1], dimensions : Dimensions [0..1], centerOfMass : Dimensions [0..1]); BulkHardware (bulkQuantity :Core/UnitofMeasure, plus two rows shaded red: /Hardware/Hardware/serialNumber : xsd:string [0] and /Core/Element/description :xsd:string [1]); and VirtualHardware (virtualHardwareModel: VirtualHardwareModelType [0..1]). A separate Dimensions class has xAxisLength, yAxisLength and zAxisLength, each : MeasureOfLength [1], and an 'Enumerations' frame holds VirtualHardwareModelType.",
