    {
      "text": "Diagrama de clases UML en un marco con la pestaña «Hardware profile». Encima del marco se sitúan Core/ Specification y Core/ Element. ProductSpecification (hazard: DefinedType [0..*]) especializa Core/Specification. La clase abstracta Hardware especializa Core/Element, con productAgent :Agent [1], hardwareVersion:xsd:string [0..1], partNumber : xsd:string [1], releaseDate :DateTime [0..1], serialNumber : xsd:string [0..1], batchNumber : xsd:string [0..1], hazard: DefinedType [0..*], category: DefinedType [0..*], additionalInformationSpecification : /Core/Specification [0..*] y additionalInformation :/Core/DictionaryEntry [0..*]. Tres clases especializan Hardware: PhysicalHardware (massOfHardware: MeasureOfMass [0..1], dimensions : Dimensions [0..1], centerOfMass : Dimensions [0..1]); BulkHardware (bulkQuantity :Core/UnitofMeasure, más dos filas sombreadas en rojo: /Hardware/Hardware/serialNumber : xsd:string [0] y /Core/Element/description :xsd:string [1]); y VirtualHardware (virtualHardwareModel: VirtualHardwareModelType [0..1]). Una clase independiente Dimensions tiene xAxisLength, yAxisLength y zAxisLength, cada uno : MeasureOfLength [1], y un marco «Enumerations» contiene VirtualHardwareModelType.",
